  "body": "So, not your fault, but I think we should propagate the error and abort the operation.\n\nThis is currently used only by dumping varlink IDL. Broken UTF8 chars should not be printed in that case.\n\nPlease consider to do something like that:\n```c\nchar32_t c;\nint n = utf8_encoded_to_unichar(p, &c);\nif (n < 0)\n        return log_debug_errno(n, ...);\n\nint cw = unichar_console_width(c);\nassert(cw >= 0);\n```\nThen, move the pointer `p` by `n` if the line is not broken.\n\nSee also #43096.",
